# tally 2.2.1 (#213, S-213), L §5.12 step 2: "An order that can't be decided (a hole) is refused (RUN-ORDER), but
# where only a window leaves it open it is HOLE-IMPRECISE (§4.4): no day of the window gives the refusal". buy_a is
# dated d_a = window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-28), buy_b 2026-02-10: under fifo the arcs' order depends on d_a, and pinned
# days give 1 000.00 or 1 200.00 PLN, so the takes and the cost are the hole naming d_a. tally 2.2 refused them
# (RUN-ORDER fill matched: the order of the arc (buy_b; sell) is a hole) (the planner's 213/f1.tally).
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): restated so the window sits in an attribute, not the movement's day: a window that
# reaches a move's `on` is a hole day (L §4.4), so the order the test is about reads the attribute.
=== f1.tally
model f1
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind funds: unit
kind trades: event certain
  leg units: funds
  leg cash: PLN
  attr seq: int
  attr bought: date
kind purchases: trades
kind sales: trades
kind pockets: place one min 0
axis method
  fifo "first in, first out"
  lifo "last in, first out"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place market: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input d_a: date
input d_a0: date
input d_b: date
input d_s: date
input n_a: num fa
input p_a: money PLN
input p_b: money PLN
input p_s: money PLN

move buy_a: purchases
  on d_a0
  attr seq = 1
  attr bought = d_a
  leg units from market to pocket amount n_a
  leg cash from konto to market amount p_a

move buy_b: purchases
  on d_b
  attr seq = 1 + 1
  attr bought = d_b
  leg units from market to pocket amount n_a
  leg cash from konto to market amount p_b

move sell: sales
  on d_s
  attr seq = 1 + 1 + 1
  attr bought = d_s
  leg units from pocket to market amount n_a
  leg cash from market to konto amount p_s

fill matched
  supply b.units.amount for b in purchases over ..
  demand x.units.amount for x in sales over ..
  arc b.bought <= x.bought
  order (if method == fifo then days_between(d_s, b.bought) else days_between(b.bought, d_s)) ties by (b.seq, x.seq)

def cost[x in sales]: money PLN = round(sum(matched.taken[b, x] * b.cash.amount / b.units.amount for b in purchases over ..), minor(PLN), half-even) at x.day

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  funds + [fa] lives 2020-01-01..
  pockets + [pocket] fa lives 2026-01-01..
  opening[konto] = 5000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[pocket] = 0 fa at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  d_a = window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-28) "s"
  d_b = 2026-02-10 "s"
  d_a0 = 2026-02-01 "s"
  d_s = 2026-03-10 "s"
  n_a = 10 fa "s"
  p_a = 1000.00 PLN "s"
  p_b = 1200.00 PLN "s"
  p_s = 1500.00 PLN "s"

ask c: cost[x] for x in sales over ..
ask c_fifo: cost[x] for x in sales over .. with method = fifo
ask t: matched.taken[b, x] for b in purchases over .., x in sales over ..
=== expect
c (x = sell) [method = *]: ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-28) not precise enough for the order of fill matched" (d_a)
  unknown day: d_a
  cut 2026-01-01
c_fifo (x = sell): ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-28) not precise enough for the order of fill matched" (d_a)
  pinned: method = fifo
  unknown day: d_a
  cut 2026-01-01
t (b = buy_a, x = sell) [method = *]: ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-28) not precise enough for the order of fill matched" (d_a)
  unknown day: d_a
  cut 2026-01-01
t (b = buy_b, x = sell) [method = *]: ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-28) not precise enough for the order of fill matched" (d_a)
  unknown day: d_a
  cut 2026-01-01
